@startuml
title C7 Zitadel roles -> Fluree identity / policy class -> policy-filtered SPARQL
participant "Zitadel" as Z
participant "FastAPI service" as API
participant "Fluree server" as FL
participant "Ledger (policies as RDF)" as LG
Z -> API : user token (sub, project roles claim)
API -> API : map roles -> policy-class IRIs, sub -> identity IRI
Z -> API : service-account JWT with custom claims via Zitadel Action
note right of API : needs fluree.ledger.read/write.* and fluree.policy = "request"
API -> FL : SPARQL + Bearer(service) + fluree-identity + fluree-policy-class headers
FL -> FL : verify JWT via JWKS; CredentialPolicy::Request trusts headers
FL -> LG : resolve identity -> f:policyClass, load policies
LG --> FL : filtered flakes (reads), checked staged flakes (writes)
FL --> API : policy-filtered results
note over API, FL : Anyone holding the service credential can impersonate any identity: protect it like a DB password
@enduml
